    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1037">

                <pb facs="1548" n="1528" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg1528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/12–1250</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of Defense</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marshall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1037-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-12-12">12 December,
                        1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Attached hereto is the statement of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, signed by General
                    Bradley, regarding the terms they feel are necessary and should be imposed
                    regarding any cease-fire settlement in Korea.</p>
                <p>I am in general agreement with the various conditions enumerated but I wish to
                    state, however, that I do not consider the contents of <pb facs="1549" n="1529"
                        xml:id="pg1529"/> Paragraph 6 should have been included in this document. I
                    am assured that the possible implication of that paragraph that the Joint Chiefs
                    of Staff felt that a continued fight for the conquest of North Korea was not the
                    purpose of the statement. Rather it was included merely to bring to the
                    attention of higher authorities the certain possibility resulting from a
                    cease-fire negotiation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1037-a1.xml" xpointer="d1037-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1037-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1037-f1-content">
                <p>This note and its enclosure were circulated on December 13 by the Executive
                    Secretary of the NSC for the information of the
                        NSC and the Secretary of the Treasury as
                        NSC 95.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
